btrfs compressed-append reclaim reproducer
==========================================

Sixteen files are appended with 17/511/4093 byte records through stdio. Every
64 records each file is fdatasync()ed and its page cache dropped with
POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED, so the next append into a partial block has to read that
block back (prepare_uptodate_folio() -> btrfs_read_folio()). The data is
highly compressible, so on a compress=zstd mount these are compressed reads.
A pressure thread and an anonymous buffer keep the 256M memory cgroup in
reclaim, which runs the btrfs extent map shrinker.

Before "btrfs: don't look up the extent map again when submitting a
compressed read", btrfs_submit_compressed_read() failed the read with -EIO
when the shrinker had dropped the extent map after btrfs_do_readpage(), and
the append returned EIO. On the J700 (compress=zstd:1 root) this reproduced
with "run.sh <dir> 25 208" at record 330 (aurora-ctl h-6198).

Pass: RESULT ... eio=0 other=0 and VERIFY bytes equal to the bytes written.
